From 80ac6d197218c3399d66674167a4d7c9051a25e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Zhang <henryzhang62@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:45:26 -0700
Subject: drm/vc4: dsi: Set the transfer result before completing the transfer
Mime-version: 1.0
Content-type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-transfer-encoding: 8bit
Git-commit: 80ac6d197218c3399d66674167a4d7c9051a25e2
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc4
References: git-fixes

On an HSTX timeout the interrupt handler completes the transfer and
only then sets xfer_result to -ETIMEDOUT. The waiter, which may run on
another CPU, can wake up and read xfer_result in between, still 0 from
the start of the transfer, and report the timed-out transfer as a
success.

Set xfer_result first. complete() orders the store before the wake-up.

Fixes: 4078f5757144 ("drm/vc4: Add DSI driver")
Signed-off-by: Henry Zhang <henryzhang62@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261028164539.3471833-2-henryzhang62@gmail.com
Reviewed-by: Maíra Canal <mcanal@igalia.com>
Signed-off-by: Maíra Canal <mcanal@igalia.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_dsi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_dsi.c
index aff50b2c5846..762929ec471f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_dsi.c
@@ -1527,8 +1527,8 @@ static irqreturn_t vc4_dsi_irq_handler(int irq, void *data)
 		complete(&dsi->xfer_completion);
 		ret = IRQ_HANDLED;
 	} else if (stat & DSI_PORT_BIT(INT_HSTX_TO)) {
-		complete(&dsi->xfer_completion);
 		dsi->xfer_result = -ETIMEDOUT;
+		complete(&dsi->xfer_completion);
 		ret = IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
